menu "Rotary encoder (drivers/encoder)"

    config ENCODER_COUNTS_PER_DETENT
        int "Default edges per detent (x4 decoding)"
        default 4
        range 1 64
        help
            4 when one click is one full quadrature cycle, which is the common
            case (Bourns PEC09: 24 pulses, 24 detents). 2 for half-cycle-per-
            detent parts; 1 for a detent-less wheel counted edge by edge.

    config ENCODER_GLITCH_NS
        int "Default glitch filter (ns)"
        default 10000
        range 0 12700
        help
            PCNT ignores pulses shorter than this. The hardware limit is 1023
            APB cycles (12.7 us at 80 MHz). Mechanical bounce outlasts this, so
            the filter is a first line only; the detent arithmetic is the second.

    config ENCODER_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Encoder task priority"
        default 8
        range 1 24
        help
            Human-timescale work, like drivers/buttons: below every SDK deadline
            task.

    config ENCODER_TASK_CORE
        int "Encoder task core affinity"
        default 0
        range 0 1

    config ENCODER_TASK_STACK
        int "Encoder task stack (bytes)"
        default 3072
        range 2048 16384
        help
            The application callback runs on this stack.

endmenu
